    "intro_html":  "Chile colorado is beef stewed in pure red chile sauce. No beans, no tomato base, no shortcuts through a can of enchilada sauce. Dried guajillos and anchos get soaked and blended, the chuck browns in flour first so the sauce clings, and then it just simmers until the beef gives up. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e36 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 570 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.59\u003c/strong\u003e.",
